      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The oxidative carbonylation of ToMCoMe (1; ToM = tris(4,4-dimethyl-2-oxazolinyl)phenylborate) involves its rapid, reversible reaction with CO to form ToMCo{C(O)Me}CO (2) followed by rapid reaction with O2 yielding ToMCoOAc (3), in contrast to the slow direct carboxylation of ToMCoMe by CO2."},
